{"title":"1979 AHSME Problems/Problem 20","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1.1_(Guiding_through_the_thought_process)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1.1 (Guiding through the thought process)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/2/cc295b23ab3707b548ca30a48b6977799841259d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=\\tfrac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"43\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/9/3892466fc4540cfe0633eb92141f26b63f7e76c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a+1)(b+1)=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"141\" height=\"18\" /> then the radian measure of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/6/396c6a8ee6f492336e6a2ff93e5fd145b2b77cb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\arctan a + \\arctan b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"147\" height=\"14\" /> equals\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/4/114274da61eab5c81f845d43544fc05286c8f2e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\qquad \\textbf{(B) }\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\qquad \\textbf{(C) }\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\qquad \\textbf{(D) }\\frac{\\pi}{5}\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }\\frac{\\pi}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"381\" height=\"33\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Solution by e_power_pi_times_i\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/3/58371499ac4be5e5fbf324de21151edfd8a2c0ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"45\" height=\"37\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/f/c9fad8257e9e94a6472e29e558a8010f44c4e15d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"43\" height=\"37\" />. Now we evaluate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/2/942fd8362d3b9a1f1124937f8511a5119de8fd4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\arctan a$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"63\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/b/0db5bb635ab9175036b445eda95b485550af9534.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\arctan b$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />. Denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/9/fb9a3ff1f0e1527da685aadc79cdfb1e9f485b1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\arctan x = \\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"96\" height=\"13\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/7/69702a09796c4dec60a9362198168056a7c1d15c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(\\arctan(x)) = \\tan(\\theta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"187\" height=\"18\" />, and simplifying gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/9/0999f31f210f69cd3ca0e9183eaa21068430abd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\tan(\\theta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"82\" height=\"18\" />. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/5/565aef6b3f3f32f9a718095f9732c74099698ede.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = \\tan(\\theta_a) = \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"126\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/6/c862f3872304b0a56e38d4fa7b0c31d8b4d0f485.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = \\tan(\\theta_b) = \\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"123\" height=\"37\" />. The question asks for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/a/01a6ebdeaf1bcc0a7b602c2895a74039fa666f7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta_a + \\theta_b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" />, so we try to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/4/89422a3849a916762c4627e63611ce0beb226011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(\\theta_a + \\theta_b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"93\" height=\"18\" /> in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/3/553d636371764b46f62178b8be12b10b19f3035f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(\\theta_a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/2/782900688cf7c5adbc53f533a73ca4e2187b5bc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(\\theta_b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" />. Using the angle addition formula for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/b/9cb465a154d67b07a4984f0377da3619ec3e0440.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(\\alpha+\\beta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" />, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/1/3711fc99099659131c30d1bad62a67ae125c981d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(\\theta_a + \\theta_b) = \\frac{\\tan(\\theta_a)+\\tan(\\theta_b)}{1-\\tan(\\theta_a)\\tan(\\theta_b)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"267\" height=\"43\" />. Plugging <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/e/bfe27e0f37b846595c3e10f8196d24f2dfebf736.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(\\theta_a) = \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"92\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/a/d6a93bb017f24685744d95f4dbf36d0fa51f142a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(\\theta_b) = \\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"91\" height=\"37\" /> in, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/6/926e706fb8d99c63c0bce07bb65b2a2861c1c95e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(\\theta_a + \\theta_b) = \\frac{\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{3}}{1-(\\frac{1}{2})(\\frac{1}{3})}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"201\" height=\"47\" />. Simplifying, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/e/4be58baf3fd398789854057da8ba742b58eb4556.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(\\theta_a + \\theta_b) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"126\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/a/01a6ebdeaf1bcc0a7b602c2895a74039fa666f7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta_a + \\theta_b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" /> in radians is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/1/4213c7f94c2cd9b12acc6f87689504c563864137.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } \\frac{\\pi}{4}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"61\" height=\"44\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1.1_.28Guiding_through_the_thought_process.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1.1_(Guiding_through_the_thought_process)\">Solution 1.1 (Guiding through the thought process)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1.1 (Guiding through the thought process)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Thinking through the problem, we can see <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/2/942fd8362d3b9a1f1124937f8511a5119de8fd4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\arctan a$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"63\" height=\"12\" /> is the angle whose tangent is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/2/192b4a258ee998961a99523fd0f0a029f9ea194a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.5$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/b/0db5bb635ab9175036b445eda95b485550af9534.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\arctan b$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" /> is the angle whose tangent is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />. Call the former angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/d/3dd2b053518a1dc68824d714682ff9df76d8f151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" />, the latter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/1/981e552986db2a6a782e1699452472a78544d757.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" />. So we are trying to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/7/297177ee4a51f87085653928859f821ba5ad2389.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta_1+\\theta_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"17\" />. So given two tangent measures, it is natural for us to think about the sum of tangent measures (what else can we try? Remember: we are not allowed to use calculators). Plug in as above and continue on.\n</p><p>~hastapasta\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME\" title=\"1979 AHSME\">1979 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1979 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1979 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1979\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"1979 AHSME Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"1979 AHSME Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1979 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?titl